# ST4Notes

Daily notes + YouTrack integration for Sublime Text 4.

Stores a single plain-text notes file (`.stnotes` / `ST4Notes` syntax), with commands to add/search entries, open tickets, import issues, and optionally post comments back to YouTrack.

## Commands (Cmd+Shift+P / Ctrl+Shift+P)

| Command | What it does |
|---------|----------------|
| **Notes: Add** | Append a timed note (ticket / TODO / OPS / create or import from YouTrack) |
| **Notes: Edit** | Open the notes file |
| **Notes: Search** | Quick-panel search over tickets / TODO / OPS |
| **Notes: Open Issue** | Open a ticket in the browser (or list YouTrack issues) |
| **Notes: Weekly Summary** | Scratch view of recent activity |
| **Notes: Weekly Search** | Search within the weekly window |
| **Notes: Create Issue** | Create a YouTrack issue (optional stage sub-tasks) |
| **Notes: Settings** | Edit package settings |

Also: **Tools → Notes**, and a few entries on the context menu.

## Notes file format

```
# ==============================================================================
# 2026.9.11
# ==============================================================================
# PROJ-1234:
- [09:15] [IN PROGRESS] shipped dry-run gate
- [10:02] [DONE]<< - follow-up with @alice #deploy
```

Syntax highlights dates, ticket IDs, state tags (`[DONE]`, `[IN REVIEW]`, …), `@mentions`, `#hashtags`, and URLs. Hover a URL or ticket ID in a notes view to open / preview.

## Settings

**Preferences → Package Settings → ST4Notes**

| Key | Default | Notes |
|-----|---------|--------|
| `notes_file` | `~/Documents/ST4Notes` | Local notes path (`~` expanded) |
| `youtrack_base` | `""` | e.g. `https://youtrack.example.com/issue/` (https only) |
| `youtrack_token` | `""` | Permanent token — **User settings only**, never commit |
| `default_project` | `""` | YouTrack project shortName |
| `issue_stages` | `[]` | Optional stage sub-task names |
| `post_comments` | `false` | Post note text as YouTrack comments on Add |
| `api_timeout_sec` | `10` | HTTP timeout |
| `api_max_retries` | `2` | Retries on 429/502/503 |

User overrides live in `Packages/User/ST4Notes.sublime-settings` and merge over package defaults.

## Install (manual)

Copy this `notes` folder into your Sublime Text `Packages` directory:

| Platform | Path |
|----------|------|
| **Windows** | `%APPDATA%\Sublime Text\Packages\` |
| **Mac** | `~/Library/Application Support/Sublime Text/Packages/` |
| **Linux** | `~/.config/sublime-text/Packages/` |

Restart Sublime Text (or Package Control: Satisfy Dependencies / reload).

**Dev symlink:**

```bash
ln -s "/path/to/sublime-text-packages/notes" \
  "$HOME/Library/Application Support/Sublime Text/Packages/notes"
```

### Migrating from Packages/User

If you previously kept `notes_plugin.py` (and related files) under `Packages/User/`, remove those copies after installing this package so commands are not registered twice:

- `notes_plugin.py`
- `notes_plugin.sublime-commands`
- `ST4Notes.sublime-syntax`
- `ST4Notes.sublime-color-scheme`
- `ST4Notes.tmPreferences`

Keep `Packages/User/ST4Notes.sublime-settings` for your token and personal overrides.

## Requirements

- Sublime Text 4
- Optional: YouTrack permanent token for create/import/comment features

## Safety

- `youtrack_base` must be `https://` (http rejected)
- Loopback / private / CGNAT / `.local` / metadata hostnames rejected
- YouTrack API calls refuse HTTP redirects (Bearer is not forwarded)
- Default `post_comments` is `false`
- Package defaults ship with an empty token
- Magic note text `DONE` / `REVIEW` asks before changing YouTrack state
- Keep tokens only in `Packages/User/ST4Notes.sublime-settings` (never commit)
